  "content": {
    "id": "p15-q5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "A function $f(x)$ is said to be self-inverse if $f(f(x))=x$. Determine which of the following are self-inverse functions.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p15-q5-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\dfrac{1}{x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Self-inverse.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(f(x))&=\\frac{1}{1/x}\\\\f(f(x))&=x\\end{align*}$$\n\nThis holds for every $x\\ne0$ in the domain, so $f$ is self-inverse.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p15-q5-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\dfrac{x}{x-1}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Self-inverse.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(f(x))&=\\frac{\\frac{x}{x-1}}{\\frac{x}{x-1}-1}\\\\f(f(x))&=\\frac{\\frac{x}{x-1}}{\\frac{1}{x-1}}\\\\f(f(x))&=x\\end{align*}$$\n\nThis holds for every $x\\ne1$ in the domain, so $f$ is self-inverse.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p15-q5-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\dfrac{x-1}{x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Not self-inverse.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(f(x))&=\\frac{\\frac{x-1}{x}-1}{\\frac{x-1}{x}}\\\\f(f(x))&=\\frac{-1/x}{(x-1)/x}\\\\f(f(x))&=-\\frac{1}{x-1}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe composition is defined for $x\\ne0,1$ and does not equal $x$ identically. Therefore $f$ is not self-inverse.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 31
      },
      {
        "id": "p15-q5-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\dfrac{x+1}{x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Not self-inverse.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(f(x))&=\\frac{\\frac{x+1}{x}+1}{\\frac{x+1}{x}}\\\\f(f(x))&=\\frac{(2x+1)/x}{(x+1)/x}\\\\f(f(x))&=\\frac{2x+1}{x+1}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe composition is defined for $x\\ne0,-1$ and does not equal $x$ identically. Therefore $f$ is not self-inverse.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 31
      }
    ]
  },
